# Human approval required for the gate surface.
#
# These paths decide whether a change is allowed to merge or deploy, or decide
# what lands on the human's machine. An agent that can rewrite them can clear
# its own path, so the gates would still run and would simply agree with
# whoever edited them last. Everything else in this repo (skills, docs, specs,
# per-plugin manifests) is deliberately left un-owned: agents work here freely.
#
# CODEOWNERS is last-match-wins, so no rule below may be widened to overlap an
# earlier one without checking what it shadows.

# Owns itself. Without this, anyone with push could delete the rules below in a
# PR that nothing gates, which is the same hole one level up.
/.github/CODEOWNERS @mujtaba3B

# The gate scripts and the hook manifests that arm them.
/eng/hooks/ @mujtaba3B
/qa/hooks/ @mujtaba3B

# The delivery mechanism, which outranks the gates it delivers. bin/install
# copies the plugins into ~/.claude/plugins/cache, bin/gstack-extensions-upgrade
# calls it, and 21 skills offer to run that upgrade, so an edit here executes on
# the human's machine during a routine "Upgrade now".
/bin/ @mujtaba3B

# The root marketplace lists which plugins exist. Dropping eng or qa from it
# stops their gates being installed at all, with no change to a gate script.
/.claude-plugin/ @mujtaba3B
